  [ERROR TTS] Slide 1: Command 'edge-tts --text "Bienvenidos a esta clase sobre Impl 36 SystemSetup Print layouts en SAP Business One. En esta lección exploraremos las mejores prácticas de consultoría, flujos operativos y configuraciones del sistema. System Setup & Administration: Print Layouts SAP Business One Version 10.0 This topic covers print layouts which are required for the printing of documents and reports." --voice es-MX-JorgeNeural --write-media temp_aud_10_Impl_36_Syst_1.mp3' returned non-zero exit status 1.
  [ERROR TTS] Slide 2: Command 'edge-tts --text "Objectives Objectives: Describe the function of a print layout Set default print layouts for users and by business partner Use the Report and Layout Manager for managing reports and print layouts Define a printing sequence for a document On completion of this topic, you will be able to: • Describe the function of a print layout • Set default print layouts for users and by business partner • Use the Report and Layout Manager for managing reports and print layouts • Define a printing sequence for a document" --voice es-MX-JorgeNeural --write-media temp_aud_10_Impl_36_Syst_2.mp3' returned non-zero exit status 1.
  [ERROR TTS] Slide 3: Command 'edge-tts --text "Print Layout Concept SAP Business One Each marketing document or report has a print layout This is a template for how the on-screen document will look in printed form Printed documents Layout Layout Print layouts are templates that define how an on-screen document or report will look when it is printed. SAP provides a set of predefined layouts for each marketing document. You can use these right out-of- the-box or you can edit them to create client-specific printed documents. This is typically done for external facing documents, but you can also customize the layouts for internally used documents such as pick lists and bills of materials. You can also create new print layouts for customized reports that you develop." --voice es-MX-JorgeNeural --write-media temp_aud_10_Impl_36_Syst_3.mp3' returned non-zero exit status 1.
  [ERROR TTS] Slide 4: Command 'edge-tts --text "Print Layouts for a Document A document can have multiple print layouts To preview a document in the available layouts, open a document and choose File > Preview Layouts… The default layout is marked in bold There can be multiple print layouts for a document. To see the available print layouts, open a document and choose the preview layouts option from the File menu. The layouts available for the current document type are shown. Then select a layout to view the printed document. The one in bold is the default template that will be used when this user prints this document. You should decide with the customer which templates will be required for each document. For example, an A/R invoice can be printed as a packing list as well as an invoice. Note: If you print or preview a document before you add it to the system, the system automatically adds the Draft watermark to the printout." --voice es-MX-JorgeNeural --write-media temp_aud_10_Impl_36_Syst_4.mp3' returned non-zero exit status 1.
  [ERROR TTS] Slide 5: Command 'edge-tts --text "Setting the Default Print Layout A default layout can be specified for all users, for the current user only, or for specified users You can also set a default for all business partners or for specified business partners Authorization required to set default layout It is quite possible that users might need to use more than one print layout template for a document. A user might need to use an invoice layout for each of their customers’ languages, or set a different invoice layout for certain groups of customers. Authorized users can set a different layout to be used as default for different users or business partners. To set the default layout, open a document and choose the Layout Designer icon from the icon toolbar. This opens a window where you can choose another layout and set as default. A new template can be set as default for:  All users  The current user only  Specific users that you select from the list of users You can also set the layout as default for:  All business partners for which a default template has not yet been assigned  Selected business partners – this allows you to select one or more business partners. Note: To be authorized to change the default print layout for a document or report, the general authorization General Change Default Report is required." --voice es-MX-JorgeNeural --write-media temp_aud_10_Impl_36_Syst_5.mp3' returned non-zero exit status 1.
  [ERROR TTS] Slide 6: Command 'edge-tts --text "Customizing Print Layouts Print layouts need to be customized to meet the customer’s needs for external facing documents You can also translate print layouts to provide documents in the customer’s native language To save time during an implementation, demonstrate the various print layouts available for a document, and identify a layout as the base for changes Print layouts need to be customized during an implementation project to meet the customer’s needs for external facing documents. You will need at minimum to insert the company’s logo and address. You might need to translate the print layout to provide printed documents in a customer’s native language. These changes can take a considerable amount of time. During an implementation you should demonstrate the various print layouts to the customer. When you identify a layout that best fits the customer’s needs, you can use that layout as the base for changes." --voice es-MX-JorgeNeural --write-media temp_aud_10_Impl_36_Syst_6.mp3' returned non-zero exit status 1.
