  [ERROR TTS] Slide 4: Command 'edge-tts --text "Concept Production std. cost is a budgeted production cost which can be compared to the actual production cost. Item Master Data Production Std Cost can be optionally set to the current valuation cost and can also be optionally rolled up through multiple levels of bill of materials. Bill of Materials window displays the Production Std. Cost data for item components, the cost data for resource components and the Production Std Cost data for the produced item. Benefit: Facilitates budget to actual cost comparisons and production variance calculations. Actual Cost Production Std. Cost Difference Copy The main idea behind this feature is to allow us to plan a budget for the production cost. Then we can compare the actual cost of a product to this budgeted cost. In addition we can copy the actual cost of the produced items in a BOM to their Production Std. Cost in an automatic procedure. When working in the Bill of Material and Production Order windows, we can see the Production Std. Cost information. In addition we can analyze the difference between the budgeted cost and the actual cost in the Inventory Audit Trail report." --voice es-MX-JorgeNeural --write-media temp_aud_10_Production_5_4.mp3' returned non-zero exit status 1.
